# ═══ Draft knowledge entry — modern cmake multi-dep cross wiring (per-dep <Name>_DIR
# preseed), SDK llvm-ranlib gap on static-lib targets, and gtest suite local execution
# from source root (data-file CWD dependency)
# Software: minizip-ng 4.2.2
# Gate: conan-verify G2 (conan create, ohos-aarch64) + upstream gtest 42/42 + W3 local green
# Status: DRAFT

id: minizip-ng-4.2.2-cmake-multidep-cross-and-gtest-local
severity: 2
category: build-system|cmake|ohos|testing
trigger_tool: cmake|conan|ctest|gtest
phase: build

keywords: find_package, CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH, FIND_ROOT_PATH, _DIR cache var, llvm-ranlib, llvm-ar, static library, gtest, FetchContent, CWD, data file, MZ_FETCH_LIBS, iconv, libbsd
error_signature: Error running link command: no such file or directory|undefined symbol: mz_os_delete_file|Which is: -111|registry probe failed|Unable to find library
match_keywords: find_package cross, _DIR preseed, llvm-ranlib missing, static lib ENOENT, gtest FetchContent offline, gtest data file CWD, monotonic, mz_os_unlink, MZ_ICONV musl

root_cause: |
  (1) Modern cmake packages that wire N dependencies through plain find_package(ZLIB /
  LibLZMA / OpenSSL / zstd / BZip2) hit the OHOS cross chain's FIND_ROOT_PATH=ONLY:
  each conan dep needs its own <Name>_DIR cache var preseeded with the real
  <pkg>/lib/cmake/<name> path — a single CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH alone is not enough when
  the toolchain sets the find modes to ONLY.
  (2) Building STATIC library targets with the OHOS SDK toolchain fails with the
  generic "Error running link command: no such file or directory": ohos.toolchain.cmake
  points CMAKE_RANLIB at $SDK/llvm/bin/llvm-ranlib which does NOT exist (only llvm-ar
  ships). The .so route (BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON) sidesteps ar/ranlib entirely; for
  recipes that must produce .a, preseed -DCMAKE_RANLIB=$(which llvm-ranlib) from
  /data/service/hnp/bin (the conan-verified recipe's _llvm_ranlib() helper).
  (3) Upstream gtest suites fetched via FetchContent cannot build on the offline CI;
  building them locally against the registry gtest/1.17.0 requires running the test
  binary from the SOURCE ROOT — stream/crypt tests open data files ("LICENSE",
  test.p12, uniform.bin) relative to CWD, and running from build/test/ returns
  MZ_OPEN_ERROR (-111) for every file-backed case.
  (4) API drift inside a lib family: minizip-ng 4.x renamed mz_os_delete_file to
  mz_os_unlink — verify exact exported symbols with readelf before writing the test.

rec_approach: per-dep-dir-preseed + so-route-or-ranlib-override + gtest-run-from-srcroot + readelf-symbol-verify
rec_description: |
  (1) In the recipe build(), for every requires() dependency resolve its package
  folder, locate lib/cmake/<name>, and append '-D<Name>_DIR=<path>' (try name,
  lower, upper variants; fall back to scanning lib/cmake entries). Combine with the
  ohos-find-deps.cmake preload (CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH/PREFIX_PATH + MODE_* BOTH) via
  -DCMAKE_PROJECT_TOP_LEVEL_INCLUDES.
  (2) Prefer BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON for the package itself; if the upstream test build
  drags in a static libminizip.a, pass -DCMAKE_RANLIB=/data/service/hnp/bin/llvm-ranlib
  AND clear the cmake cache (a stale CMakeCache keeps the old broken ranlib path in
  link.txt even after the -D changes).
  (3) For upstream gtest suites on CI-offline packages: build the test executable
  locally against registry gtest (cmake -DGTEST_ROOT/-DGTEST_LIBRARY/-DGTest_DIR +
  -DMZ_FETCH_LIBS=OFF style switches), then execute it with CWD = source root so the
  data files resolve; LD_LIBRARY_PATH needs the SDK libc++ dir and the openssl conan
  package lib dir.
  (4) Before writing test_package sources, readelf --dyn-syms the built .so and match
  every API you call against real exports.
  (5) MZ_ICONV=OFF on musl (no iconv); MZ_LIBBSD=OFF to stop the cross find_package
  from guessing bogus relative paths.

rec_commands:
  - "conan create archives/m/minizip-ng/4.2.2 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing"
  - "readelf -W --dyn-syms <pkg>/lib/libminizip.so | grep mz_os_unlink  # verify before test"

verification: |
  conan create on ohos-aarch64 (clang 15) green: libminizip.so 4.9MB + include/minizip/
  packaged and signed; test_package 9/9 (writer add_buffer deflate -> reader locate/
  open/read roundtrip). Upstream gtest suite built from registry gtest/1.17.0 and run
  from source root: 42/42 PASSED, 0 FAILED (exit 0), including stream/encrypt/compat/
  path suites.

related:
  - archives/l/libzip/1.11.4/conanfile.py (ohos-find-deps + ranlib helper precedent)
  - archives/l/libzippp/7.1-1.10.1/conanfile.py (per-dep cache preseed precedent)
  - knowledge/graph/ (llvm-ranlib gap family, E-series)
